EchoZone is a '''location-based''', '''anonymous''' social media platform inspired by ''Yik Yak'', designed for real-time local discussions and community interaction. It allows users to post short messages visible only within a defined '''geographic radius'''. The platform aims to provide a unique experience for users to engage with their local community. 

== Overview ==
EchoZone is a social media platform that enables users to share their thoughts and opinions anonymously, with a focus on location-based discussions. The platform is currently in '''early development''', with a planned '''tech stack''' that includes '''React''', '''Node.js''', '''Firebase''', '''Mapbox''', and more.

=== Core Features ===
The platform offers several key features, including:
* '''Anonymous posting''': allowing users to share their thoughts without revealing their identity
* '''Location-based feed''': showing users posts from their surrounding area
* '''Upvotes and downvotes''': enabling users to interact with posts and influence their visibility
* '''Real-time updates''': providing a dynamic and engaging experience for users
* '''Content moderation tools''': helping to maintain a safe and respectful environment for users

== Features ==
The platform's features are designed to facilitate real-time local discussions and community interaction. Some of the key features include:
* '''Location-based''' posting and feed
* '''Anonymous''' posting and interaction
* '''Real-time''' updates and notifications
* '''Content moderation''' tools for a safe and respectful environment

== Technical Details ==
The planned '''tech stack''' for EchoZone includes:
* '''Frontend''': '''React''' / '''React Native'''
* '''Backend''': '''Node.js''' + '''Express'''
* '''Realtime Data''': '''Firebase''' / '''WebSockets'''
* '''Maps & Location''': '''Mapbox'''
* '''Authentication''': '''Anonymous''' / '''Device-based'''

